# the PE/COFF reader, bytes into the PE/COFF model
#
# a regular object, a bigobj and a PE32 or PE32+ image all read through the
# shared parse shell. the reader decides which body each section gets: the
# sections of an image that data directories name are tiled by typed pieces,
# one per structure, with raw pieces between, and every other section is held
# raw. a section whose bytes overlap another extent is overlaid. the extents it
# produces tile the whole file, the DOS stub, gaps, padding and data outside
# every section included, so a writer gives back every input byte. every
# declared count, offset, size and address is untrusted: sums and products go
# through checked arithmetic, every string offset is checked against the string
# table and every address a structure follows is mapped to a section.

